# Rotten branch (#349, D80): the branch skin of FallingPlatform, native 32x16. intact is the at-rest cue (dead grey wood
# tapering to a broken tip, a split with a pale splinter mid-top, one dry leaf under the tip; #556); crumble1 and crumble2
# are the D7 telegraph, as the log's. The -left frames are the same branch on the left of a trunk. Not the FallingBranch
# (tan, violet leaves, overhead).
# Joint (D122, D130, 2026-11-24, the author: "the left branch is a completely different colour and has an obvious cut"): the root
# (columns 0-6) ramps from the grey wood through a half step (5 6 7) into the trunk's red-brown bark (1 2 3 4) and flares a row up
# and down into a collar; the rot and the split stay along the length, none at the joint. Keys 1-7 are kept out of the moon rim.
